<%# locals: (title:, description: nil) %>
<%# A form opened over the page you're on (the New button on an index, into the layout's modal
    frame), so making a record doesn't lose your place: ui :dialog, open as it arrives. The form
    inside submits in the frame: refused, the modal comes back with what was typed and why; saved,
    the new record's row joins the list you're on (a stream that also empties the frame, closing
    this), or for a record whose next step is on its own page (new work), you go there (the
    frame's breaks-out behavior). Esc, the ✕ or Cancel closes it, and the frame empties
    (empties-on-close), so Back never brings it up again. %>
<turbo-frame id="modal">
  <%= ui :dialog, id: "modal_dialog", open: true, title: title, description: description, size: :lg, class: "record-modal" do %>
    <%= yield %>
  <% end %>
</turbo-frame>
